ede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids November to December came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025, on that same middle, September to October came in at 47% of normal and January to February at 19%. Grid 28944 had its driest year in 1958 at 53% of normal. The preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 on grid 28944 sits at 141.2, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
